    "gold_solution": "```python\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"Disaster_Response_Logistics\")\n    m.setParam(\"TimeLimit\", 300)  # Set time limit to 300 seconds\n\n    # Data\n    depots = list(range(3))  # D0..D2\n    units = list(range(4))  # U0..U3\n    supplies = list(range(2))  # S0..S1\n    days = list(range(1))  # Day0..Day0\n\n    demands = [[[35.45], [36.33]], [[17.96], [15.87]], [[41.3], [23.02]], [[27.08], [34.53]]]\n    depot_supplies = [[[35.47], [34.19]], [[47.72], [35.36]], [[32.64], [32.53]]]\n    transport_costs = [[2.07, 4.34, 4.85, 4.27], [3.08, 2.91, 2.02, 4.32], [1.51, 2.78, 4.61, 1.6]]\n    risk_costs = [[139.78, 88.95, 195.95, 179.6], [160.83, 67.79, 85.97, 171.96], [177.76, 195.55, 172.75, 92.72]]\n    supply_volumes = [0.7, 0.86]\n    penalty_costs = [66.58, 59.52]\n    vehicle_cost = 10.0\n    vehicle_capacity = 100.0\n    total_vehicles = 20\n\n    # Decision variables\n    # Flow_D{d}_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}: Amount of supply s from depot d to unit u on day t\n    flows = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                for s in supplies:\n                    flows[(d, u, s, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Flow_D{d}_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Slack_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}: Shortage of supply s at unit u on day t\n    slacks = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for u in units:\n            for s in supplies:\n                slacks[(u, s, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Slack_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Veh_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}: Number of vehicles on route d->u on day t\n    vehicles = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                vehicles[(d, u, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.INTEGER, name=f\"Veh_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Route_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}: Route d->u is active on day t (binary)\n    routes = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                routes[(d, u, t)] = m.addVar(vtype=GRB.BINARY, name=f\"Route_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Objective: Minimize total cost (transport + penalty + vehicle + risk)\n    obj = quicksum(\n        transport_costs[d][u] * flows[(d, u, s, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units for s in supplies\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        penalty_costs[s] * slacks[(u, s, t)]\n        for t in days for u in units for s in supplies\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        vehicle_cost * vehicles[(d, u, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        risk_costs[d][u] * routes[(d, u, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units\n    )\n    m.setObjective(obj, GRB.MINIMIZE)\n\n    # Depot capacity constraints: Total outflow <= supply\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for s in supplies:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(flows[(d, u, s, t)] for u in units) <= depot_supplies[d][s][t],\n                    name=f\"DepotCap_D{d}_S{s}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Demand constraints: Inflow + slack >= demand\n    for t in days:\n        for u in units:\n            for s in supplies:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(flows[(d, u, s, t)] for d in depots) + slacks[(u, s, t)] >= demands[u][s][t],\n                    name=f\"Demand_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Vehicle capacity constraints: Total volume <= vehicles * capacity\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(supply_volumes[s] * flows[(d, u, s, t)] for s in supplies) <= vehicle_capacity * vehicles[(d, u, t)],\n                    name=f\"VehCap_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Route activation constraints: vehicles <= total_vehicles * route\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    vehicles[(d, u, t)] <= total_vehicles * routes[(d, u, t)],\n                    name=f\"RouteAct_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Fleet size constraints: Total vehicles <= total_vehicles\n    for t in days:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(vehicles[(d, u, t)] for d in depots for u in units) <= total_vehicles,\n            name=f\"FleetSize_Day{t}\"\n        )\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
    "LLM_description": "Situation:\nA severe storm has disrupted ground lines of communication across the operational area. Bridges are compromised, several corridors are intermittently contested, and flooding has rerouted civilian traffic onto narrow secondary roads. Supply Depot Alpha (airport-adjacent), Supply Depot Bravo (rail-linked), and Forward Logistics Base Charlie (port-adjacent) hold mixed relief stocks awaiting forward movement. The Northern Relief Task Force, Coastal Field Hospital, Eastern Shelter Cluster, and Highlands Distribution Team require immediate resupply of critical commodities (e.g., medical and food items) within the current operational period. Route access changes rapidly with weather and security posture, necessitating deliberate corridor selection and convoy discipline.\n\nMission:\nDeliver priority life-sustaining commodities from the listed depots to the designated field units during this operational period while minimizing total operational cost, balancing delivery speed, security risk, and resource constraints.\n\nExecution/Concept:\n- Commodities: Allocate multi-commodity flows from each depot within available stocks to meet unit requirements. Any unmet demand will be recorded as shortfall and carries a penalty to reflect humanitarian impact.\n- Routing and Risk: Each origin\u2013destination corridor must be deliberately activated before movement. Activating a route (sending any vehicles) incurs a fixed Risk Cost representing escorts, route clearance, and coordination overhead, independent of the number of vehicles deployed on that route during the period.\n- Transport Costs: Variable transport costs apply per unit moved by corridor. Vehicle deployment also carries a per-vehicle operational cost.\n- Capacity: Supply volumes consume vehicle capacity; shipments on any corridor cannot exceed vehicle capacity multiplied by vehicles assigned to that corridor. Vehicles may only operate on active routes. Total vehicles deployed across all routes cannot exceed the fleet available.\n- Prioritization: Concentrate flows on the safest, highest-throughput corridors to reduce fixed risk exposures and avoid dispersing the fleet across many low-volume lanes. Maintain flexibility to switch corridors if access degrades.\n- Constraints: Depot throughput is limited by stock availability; forward demand must be met to the maximum feasible extent; hazardous terrain, curfews, and weather windows may restrict movement timing.\n\nAnnex A - Logistics Data:\nUnit Demands (Units x Supplies):\nUnit\\Supply | S 0 | S 1\n-----------------------\nU 0        |  35.45 |  36.33\nU 1        |  17.96 |  15.87\nU 2        |  41.30 |  23.02\nU 3        |  27.08 |  34.53\nDepot Supplies (Depots x Supplies):\nDepot\\Supply | S 0 | S 1\n------------------------\nD 0        |  35.47 |  34.19\nD 1        |  47.72 |  35.36\nD 2        |  32.64 |  32.53\nTransport Costs (Depot x Unit):\nDepot\\Unit | U 0 | U 1 | U 2 | U 3\n----------------------------------\nD 0        |   2.07 |   4.34 |   4.85 |   4.27\nD 1        |   3.08 |   2.91 |   2.02 |   4.32\nD 2        |   1.51 |   2.78 |   4.61 |   1.60\nRisk Costs (Depot x Unit):\nDepot\\Unit | U 0 | U 1 | U 2 | U 3\n----------------------------------\nD 0        | 139.78 |  88.95 | 195.95 | 179.60\nD 1        | 160.83 |  67.79 |  85.97 | 171.96\nD 2        | 177.76 | 195.55 | 172.75 |  92.72\nPenalty Costs per Unit Shortage: [Supply S0: 66.58, Supply S1: 59.52]\nVolume per Supply Unit: [Supply S0: 0.7, Supply S1: 0.86]\nFleet Parameters: Cost 10.0, Capacity 100.0, Total 20",
    "LLM_description_template": "Situation:\nA severe storm has disrupted ground lines of communication across the operational area. Bridges are compromised, several corridors are intermittently contested, and flooding has rerouted civilian traffic onto narrow secondary roads. Supply Depot Alpha (airport-adjacent), Supply Depot Bravo (rail-linked), and Forward Logistics Base Charlie (port-adjacent) hold mixed relief stocks awaiting forward movement. The Northern Relief Task Force, Coastal Field Hospital, Eastern Shelter Cluster, and Highlands Distribution Team require immediate resupply of critical commodities (e.g., medical and food items) within the current operational period. Route access changes rapidly with weather and security posture, necessitating deliberate corridor selection and convoy discipline.\n\nMission:\nDeliver priority life-sustaining commodities from the listed depots to the designated field units during this operational period while minimizing total operational cost, balancing delivery speed, security risk, and resource constraints.\n\nExecution/Concept:\n- Commodities: Allocate multi-commodity flows from each depot within available stocks to meet unit requirements. Any unmet demand will be recorded as shortfall and carries a penalty to reflect humanitarian impact.\n- Routing and Risk: Each origin\u2013destination corridor must be deliberately activated before movement. Activating a route (sending any vehicles) incurs a fixed Risk Cost representing escorts, route clearance, and coordination overhead, independent of the number of vehicles deployed on that route during the period.\n- Transport Costs: Variable transport costs apply per unit moved by corridor. Vehicle deployment also carries a per-vehicle operational cost.\n- Capacity: Supply volumes consume vehicle capacity; shipments on any corridor cannot exceed vehicle capacity multiplied by vehicles assigned to that corridor. Vehicles may only operate on active routes. Total vehicles deployed across all routes cannot exceed the fleet available.\n- Prioritization: Concentrate flows on the safest, highest-throughput corridors to reduce fixed risk exposures and avoid dispersing the fleet across many low-volume lanes. Maintain flexibility to switch corridors if access degrades.\n- Constraints: Depot throughput is limited by stock availability; forward demand must be met to the maximum feasible extent; hazardous terrain, curfews, and weather windows may restrict movement timing.\n\nAnnex A - Logistics Data:\n{DEMANDS}\n{DEPOT_SUPPLIES}\n{TRANSPORT_COSTS}\n{RISK_COSTS}\n{PENALTY_COSTS}\n{SUPPLY_VOLUMES}\nFleet Parameters: Cost {VEHICLE_COST}, Capacity {VEHICLE_CAPACITY}, Total {TOTAL_VEHICLES}"
